1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:02,060
An effective director will of course be alert

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:05,240
and inquisitive, will ask tough questions without being

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:08,580
disrespectful to others such that they don't put

4
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,840
management in a defensive position.

5
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:14,260
Directors should always be reminded that alongside management

6
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,740
they are supposed to be facing the same

7
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:22,240
direction and being careful not to put the

8
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,980
executives on the defensive, can challenge and should

9
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:31,140
challenge management assumptions without necessarily again putting them

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:31,980
on the defensive.

11
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:36,420
Another key element of board effectiveness is the

12
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:37,000
board agenda.

13
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:39,820
What is on the board agenda or what

14
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:41,020
should be on the board agenda?

15
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,340
One of the ways to streamline the board

16
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,580
agenda is to ensure that there's a delegation

17
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,000
of authority document that defines what matters come

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,420
to the board for approval, those are matters

19
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,400
that should feature on the board's agenda.

20
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:58,840
Matters that have been delegated to management shouldn't

21
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:01,540
feature on the board agenda but can come

22
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:04,099
to the board by way of reporting and

23
00:01:04,099 --> 00:01:07,420
matters that are totally at the remit of

24
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:09,760
management and should only come to the board,

25
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:11,580
shouldn't even come to the board at all

26
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:13,780
either by way of information or otherwise.

27
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:18,520
So this helps to streamline the board's agenda

28
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:21,380
but typically matters that should be on the

29
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:24,760
board agenda relate to accountability, these essentially are

30
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,060
things that have happened in the past.

31
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,300
So we're reporting from quarter to quarter, we're

32
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,820
reporting for instance on the accounts, on for

33
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:37,160
instance performance over the quarter, yes that should

34
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,940
feature in the director's report to the board.

35
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:43,820
Matters of control, risk management, internal control and

36
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:46,000
all of those are again issues that have

37
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,400
happened in the past.

38
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,360
More future focused matters where the board should

39
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,880
spend most of its time are around strategy,

40
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:57,860
around the culture of the organisation, foresight, things

41
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:00,960
around foresight, those are things that many boards

42
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,000
don't spend too much time on but those

43
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,600
are things that can actually impact the quality

44
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,240
of board decisions and the quality of board

45
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:09,919
deliberations.

46
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,900
So whilst it might be difficult for the

47
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,960
board to look at each of these items

48
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:17,060
at a typical board meeting, the board plan

49
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:19,620
for the year should feature all of these

50
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:22,000
items that have been discussed.

51
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,960
Another element of board effectiveness is the board's

52
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:31,320
ability to identify and deal with dysfunctional directors.

53
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:34,660
What are some of the qualities of dysfunctionality?

54
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:37,540
A director that is often absent at board

55
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:40,560
meetings, is always unprepared for meetings, they don't

56
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,520
read their board papers, they don't do any

57
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,240
research ahead of such meetings, never willing to

58
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,380
offer a dissenting view, they agree with everything

59
00:02:47,380 --> 00:02:50,020
that is said and never declares a conflict

60
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:50,460
of interest.

61
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,360
So you have a director who is consistently

62
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,400
interested in matters on the agenda but never

63
00:02:55,400 --> 00:03:01,380
discloses such interests, that person is dysfunctional and

64
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:05,780
disruptive, has an overbearing or domineering style, they

65
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:08,040
always want to have the last word and

66
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:11,980
clearly such position always suppresses dissent or diversity

67
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:12,560
of opinion.
